-- introduction: 
---

= Dry-brine the chicken

Mix approximately @salt{4%tbsp} and @baking powder{2%tbsp} in a small bowl.

Lay @chicken leg quarters{4} on a wire rack or similar (need air contact on all sides of the chicken).

Coat the chicken in the salt/powder mixture on all sides and let sit at room temp for ~{30%min} or several hours in the fridge.

= Rub

Combine @anchor chile powder{1.5%tsp}, @dried oregano{1%tsp}, @cloves{0.5%tsp}(ground), @cinnamon{0.5%tsp}, @garlic cloves{2}(minced), @apple cider vinegar{3%tbsp}, @orange juice{1/4%cup}, and @salt{1%tsp} in a bowl.  

= Grill

When the chicken and rub are ready, heat the grill to 350 deg F and add the chicken skin down.


Flip every 10 minutes until the internal temperature is high enough.\
> Watch for flare ups, they can quickly char your chicken skin more than you want.


Remove from grill and let rest.

= Oven

Alternatively, roast in the oven for ~{25%min} and finish with a ~{5%min} broil to crisp the skin.